<title>MALAYSIA: Shell to sign new Malaysia contract.</title>
<headline>Shell to sign new Malaysia contract.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Malaysian national oil concern Petronas said on Wednesday it will sign a production sharing contract with Shell Malaysia to explore and produce oil in three new offshore blocks.</p>
<p>In a news advisory about the contract signing ceremony to be held on Friday, Petronas said the agreement would be between Shell Malaysia, a unit of Royal Dutch Shell, and Petronas Carigali Sdn Bhd, the Malaysian firm's exploration unit.</p>
<p>A spokesman at Petronas declined to provide any details on the contract and would not say where the blocks are located.</p>
<p>In January, Petronas signed a production sharing pact with Shell to develop five gas fields off the East Malaysia state of Sarawak.</p>
<p>-- Kuala Lumpur newsroom (603 206 2323)</p>
</text>
